@startuml
title Emergency Snapshot Execution

skinparam shadowing false

actor Operator
participant "CLI" as CLI
participant "Orchestrator" as Orchestrator
participant "ansible-inventory" as Inventory
participant "SSH transport" as SSH
participant "Node collector" as Node
participant "Kubernetes collector" as Kubernetes
participant "Kubernetes API" as API
participant "Prometheus" as Prometheus
participant "Report builder" as Report
participant "Manifest writer" as Manifest
database "Collection directory" as Output

Operator -> CLI : snapshot options
CLI -> CLI : Load and validate configuration
CLI -> Orchestrator : run_snapshot(...)
Orchestrator -> Inventory : --list --export
Inventory --> Orchestrator : Validated host list
Orchestrator -> Orchestrator : Check central disk reserve\nBuild temporary kdiag.pyz

par Each node, bounded by parallelism
  Orchestrator -> SSH : collect_node(...)
  SSH -> Node : SCP kdiag.pyz
  SSH -> Node : sudo -n python3.8\nnode-snapshot
  Node -> Node : Run bounded read-only checks
  Node --> SSH : gzip JSON on stdout
  SSH -> Output : node-<host>.json.gz
  SSH -> Node : Remove temporary kdiag.pyz
end

Orchestrator -> Kubernetes : collect(...)
par Three bounded read-only query groups
  Kubernetes -> API : kubectl get / get --raw
  API --> Kubernetes : Projected resources and readiness
end
Kubernetes -> API : Approved bounded Pod logs
API --> Kubernetes : Current and previous logs
Kubernetes -> Output : kubernetes.json.gz

Orchestrator -> Prometheus : Optional bounded HTTP request
Prometheus --> Orchestrator : Evidence or unavailable status
Orchestrator -> Output : prometheus.json.gz\ncollection.json

Orchestrator -> Report : build_report(...)
Report -> Output : normalized events, facts,\nfindings, JSON and Markdown reports
Orchestrator -> Manifest : write_manifest(...)
Manifest -> Output : manifest.json
Orchestrator --> CLI : Collection path and complete/partial status
CLI --> Operator : Path and exit code 0/1
@enduml
